{
  "build": "1.9.35, 03.10.2026: source-only пакет. Для FM+ STAT/PAR/DYN сохранены шесть selectable FRQ/BPM renderer IDs 0..5; historical raw IDs 6..8 normalised в MNM FRQ. Schema 42 снимает неработающий DLY CORE из menu/runtime/shipping Source: selector снова mnm|old|new, а saved CORE value 3 из schema 40/41 мигрирует в NEW=2. Schema 44 introduced persisted DFB BASE CURVE/HOLD @64 controls; current schema-45 law keeps their IDs but makes DYNAMICS RAW=63 exact unity, shapes only RAW 0..62 with BASE CURVE, uses HOLD@64=1..65/64 (fresh 65/64) as the first over-unity entry, and retains RAW/64 from RAW=65. RAW <=63 is a hard bypass of follower, governor and OLD/MNM/NEW final write clip; RAW >=64 is the active GUARD window with four LVL anchors (START/PLT @64 and @127) and common OFFSET. Fresh BASE/GUARD defaults: CURVE=.55, HOLD@64=65/64; START@64=0, PLT@64=.05, START@127=0, PLT@127=3.46, OFFSET=.18, CURVE=1.08, AMOUNT=2, ATTACK=1 ms, RELEASE=1 ms; DYNAMICS, both DSND FB INVERT, RETURN COMP and FB CLIP ON. Schema <44 migration still adds CURVE=1 and HOLD@64=1 as the safe lower entry; schema-39 anchors and schema-40 raw GUARD ID remain safe state compatibility IDs. Guard 65x257 LUT and BASE LUT rebuild only on a changed sanitized snapshot, never every audio block. DFB RMB panel remains a white 400x386 pinned child overlay inside VST, with no X, native OS window or edge jitter; repaint 10 Hz. DBAS/DWID 12 dB response, CHOR Native/Core, FM и Phaser contracts не менялись. Выполнен только static audit; full build, VST3/DAW, render и executable tests не заявляются. ARP UI follow-up: redundant PAGE 1..64 canvas caption removed, SONG toggle text label hidden while its control/tooltip remains, COPY/PASTE first popup item is WHOLE PAGE, and all PluginEditor function tooltip payloads use English/ASCII because the pixel tooltip font cannot display Cyrillic. MOD ENV UI follow-up: held-LMB crossing between AMP/FIL/MOD categories now commits selection atomically; compact MOD ENV uses the AMP/FIL 387x236 shell and control grid, without its former MATRIX/RMB/page-route mini labels. MOD ENV1..4 selection and ROUTE TO remain on the retained RMB large page. Schema 45: each P1/P2 direct LFO owns persistent UNI/BI, INV and ALT DUAL; fresh DPTH is 0, normal range 0..127 and ALT DUAL opens -127..+127. P2 direct DEST uses target-local offsets instead of raw target modulo; MOD MATRIX adds rN_inv, two collapsible INTERNAL LFO groups and hover target preview. Legacy direct DPTH values are intentionally reset to 0 during schema-45 migration. LFO timing correction restores final TRIG=HALF (raw 4) for all independent P1/P2 LFO groups: it restarts at phase 0, stops exactly at half cycle and retains its final output. SPD is now linear and tempo-relative with MULT=1X..64X: full-cycle 1/16 steps = 2048/(SPD*MULT), cycles/s = BPM*SPD*MULT/30720; the former exponential SPD curve is removed. Only source/static audit was run. LFO faceplate correction keeps PAGE/DEST target-local values at readable pixel scale, moves/enlarges the P1/P2 side badge, and anchors WAVE/choice popups to the originating cell using global screen bounds; no visual runtime render was run. Dynamic LFO SPD hover tooltip uses currentBpm() for live BPM plus active SPD/MULT; it reports 1/16, seconds, Hz, HALF and 2048/(SPD*MULT), guards SPD=0, updates with cache at UI 20 Hz, and remains English/ASCII; no visual runtime render was run. LFO LOCKS second PAGE column now reserves a non-selectable English/ASCII P2 PITCH N/A spacer; visible rows 1..10 still map exactly to PAGE 11..20, so lock/solo/state/routing and all 21 choices remain unchanged. Windows MSVC feedback found JUCE 8 C2665 on four legacy PopupMenu addCustomItem calls; they now use a PopupMenu::Item helper preserving custom hover preview, enabled/ticked state and IDs. No post-fix Windows build is claimed; rerun Release x64 VST3 is the next gate. Matrix corrective feedback: direct-LFO DPTH uses the original PAN-equivalent centred 52x43 rotary geometry and full centred LCD strip, while UNI/INV stay relative to that unchanged knob and never consume its LCD width. Direct P1-LFO DEST faceplate now reduces an already P1-prefix-compacted bank/LFO name (AMP PORT or LFO1 DPTH) to its leaf control (PORT or DPTH); dropdowns, LOCKS and Matrix names/IDs stay unchanged. Direct PAGE/DEST LCD uses its full 91px cell width so five-glyph PITCH retains scale 3 like SYNT; DPTH retains its normal PAN 87px inset. Only redundant P1-on-P1 text is compacted; P2 badge/canonical names remain visible in faceplate popup/locks/Matrix. P2 AMP DIST/VOL/PAN use IDs 144/145/146. Matrix SOURCE names use P1/P2 LFO without `INTERNAL`; readable DEPTH/POLAR widths and `POLAR` header are restored. Bottom-pinned MatrixLfoDock has a white divider and P1/P2 PARAM/LFO PAGE folders. Fresh/clear/target-picked routes are ON but DEPTH=0/DEST=OFF remain inert; MSEG/patchcord allocation chooses an unlocked blank payload before legacy disabled rows. RESET ALL queues only changed APVTS values in ordered 12-notification async chunks after one undo snapshot; host-visible value notifications are retained, undo/redo waits for completion and editor destruction flushes a pending queue. Matrix/RESET verification is source-only; no post-change build, runtime UI, VST3/DAW, DSP test or render is claimed. Matrix dock selector follow-up 04.10.2026: из expanded P1/P2 internal-LFO dock удалены redundant SETUP/DPTH SETUP; RMB DEPTH setup сохранён. Обычный LMB click открывает прежние menus, а vertical LMB drag шагами 8 px листает dock PAGE/DEST и Matrix SOURCE/DEST/AUX без popup на release; один APVTS gesture охватывает каждый реальный drag. RMB mini-panel follow-up 04.10.2026: direct-LFO DPTH RMB is a compact 228x121 SET with only UNI/BI, INV and ALT DUAL controls; redundant 0..127/full-depth/readout text is removed while main DPTH geometry/LCD and all parameter IDs/state remain unchanged. FLOATING_PANEL_FOREGROUND_TEXT_CONTRACT makes every pinnable FloatingPanel paint title/status text through final post-child paintOverChildren(), so DTIM, DFB, FILTER EXTRA, DPTH and the other mini-panels retain text after pinning. Obsolete DSND RMB popup is removed; DSND polarity/inversion remains in DFB. Extra callouts use a collection: pinned different controls coexist, transient panels still close normally, same-kind/DFB cleanup stays targeted. Static/source-only audit only; no build, DSP test, VST3/DAW test or render is claimed. DFB RAW63 UNITY corrective pass 04.10.2026: DYNAMICS now returns exact unity at RAW=63, so its BASE curve cannot attenuate the endless reference tail. FB CLIP/GUARD and every final write stabiliser are a hard RAW>=64 path; RAW=64 is the first over-unity entry (HOLD @64 fresh 65/64) and RAW=65+ retains RAW/64. Guard ownership is shared by LUT/follower/OLD/MNM/NEW write paths. Parameter IDs, automation routes, schema 45, DLY modes and embedded DFB UI remain retained. Source/static audit only; no build, DSP test, VST3/DAW test or render is claimed. ENV held-LMB release commit 04.10.2026: PixelButton now masks the originating onClick while Button mouseUp performs release cleanup after a real drag. Compact AMP/FIL ENV/MOD ENV and retained large tabs keep the last crossed target category; normal clicks and IDs/state/DSP remain unchanged. Source/static audit only; no build, UI/DSP test, VST3/DAW validation or render is claimed. FloatingPanel foreground ink correction 04.10.2026: common post-child compositor explicitly resets white ink before paintFloatingForeground, because pixel text draws with the current Graphics colour. DTIM/DPTH static labels and FILTER/DFB titles/footers remain readable pinned and unpinned; pin/drag/children/IDs/state/DSP are unchanged. Source/static audit only; no build, UI/DSP test, VST3/DAW validation or render is claimed.",
